      "id": "3jffa8h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Force"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Force is a vector quantity defined as the external agency that changes or tends to change the state of rest or uniform motion of a body.",
        "Newton's First Law introduces the concept of inertia, while the Second Law provides the quantitative formula for force (F = ma).",
        "Work is a scalar quantity calculated as the dot product of force and displacement (W = F × s × cos θ).",
        "Power is defined as the rate of doing work or energy consumption per unit time (P = W / t).",
        "Work done on an object is zero whenever the applied force is perpendicular to displacement or when total displacement is zero."
      ],
      "id": "v33atth"
    },
